1. Introduction

This Technical Specification defines the system architecture, hardware components, software interfaces, and performance requirements for the Orbital Star Ring Smart City, a self‑governing toroidal habitat in Low Earth Orbit (LEO). The habitat’s intelligence is implemented through the QUENNE Stacked Intelligence framework, a nine‑layer cognitive architecture that aligns ethical governance, domain‑specific AI, hybrid computing, and open‑source foundations.

The document is intended for systems engineers, hardware designers, software architects, and mission planners. It provides the technical baseline for prototyping, procurement, integration, and verification.

---

2. System Overview

Orbital Star Ring

· Geometry: Torus, major radius 500 m (ring centreline), minor radius 50 m (tube diameter).
· Circumference: ~3,142 m.
· Pressurised Volume: ~2.5×10⁶ m³.
· Nominal Crew/Residents: 10,000.
· Orbit: 550 km, circular, 51.6° inclination (ISS compatible).
· Rotation Rate: 1.2 rpm (provides 0.4 g at outer rim).

QUENNE Stack – Mapping to Physical Subsystems
Each of the nine layers is instantiated as one or more dedicated subsystems with well‑defined interfaces. The stack is strictly layered; each layer provides services exclusively to the layer above and consumes services exclusively from the layer below.

