3. Layer 9: Human Authority – Triad AI Core

3.1 Functional Requirements

· FR‑9.1 – Enforce ethical, strategic, and protective axioms on all lower‑layer decisions.
· FR‑9.2 – Maintain a digital twin of the entire habitat with <1 s latency.
· FR‑9.3 – Conduct reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF) with resident referenda.
· FR‑9.4 – Provide explainability interfaces for all overrides.

3.2 Hardware Specification

· Three independent high‑assurance server nodes (Michael, Gabriel, Rafael), physically separated, each with:
  · 2× 64‑core RISC‑V vector CPUs (space‑rated, 2 GHz).
  · 1× Tensor Core accelerator (e.g., NVIDIA Jetson Orin‑class, rad‑hard).
  · 512 GB ECC RAM, 10 TB NVMe storage.
  · Redundant MIL‑STD‑1553 and 10 GbE fibre interfaces.
· Triad voting logic implemented in triple‑modular redundant (TMR) FPGAs.

3.3 Software Stack

· OS: Real‑time Linux with PREEMPT_RT, seL4 microkernel on secure partitions.
· Digital Twin: Unity + custom physics engine, updated via City‑wide Sensor Fusion Engine.
· RLHF: Federated learning aggregator, differential privacy.
· Ethical Constraint API: gRPC with mutual TLS, every call includes proof of compliance.

3.4 Performance Targets

· Decision latency (ethical audit): <10 ms.
· Digital twin state convergence: <100 ms.
· Throughput: 50,000 constraint checks per second.

