4. Layer 8: Nuclear Intelligence – Fusion Reactor Control System

4.1 Functional Requirements

· FR‑8.1 – Autonomous control of 12 compact fusion reactors (helium‑3 / deuterium).
· FR‑8.2 – Plasma stability maintenance (β limit, confinement time).
· FR‑8.3 – Fuel cycle management: tritium breeding, helium‑3 extraction, waste handling.
· FR‑8.4 – Certification to IEC 61508 SIL‑4, DO‑178C DAL A.

4.2 Hardware Specification

· Reactor Controller: 3× radiation‑hardened PowerPC e5500, lockstep.
· Sensors: Magnetic probes, interferometers, neutron flux detectors.
· Actuators: Gyrotrons, gas injection valves, magnetic coil power supplies.
· Interconnect: SpaceWire, time‑triggered Ethernet (TTEthernet).

4.3 Software Stack

· OS: Deployed on seL4, formally verified.
· Plasma control algorithm: Real‑time nonlinear MPC, 10 kHz cycle.
· Safety monitor: Independent watchdog, diverse programming.

4.4 Performance Targets

· Plasma response time: <50 µs.
· Reactor trip (emergency shutdown): <2 ms.
· Mean time between unscheduled maintenance: >10,000 h.

