5. Layer 7: Atomic Fusion – City‑wide Sensor Fusion Engine

5.1 Functional Requirements

· FR‑7.1 – Ingest and fuse data from >100,000 sensors (10 Hz – 1 kHz).
· FR‑7.2 – Produce a probabilistic world model with uncertainty quantification.
· FR‑7.3 – Detect anomalies and predict near‑future states.
· FR‑7.4 – Provide query interface for higher layers.

5.2 Hardware Specification

· Fusion Cluster: 8× GPU nodes (NVIDIA A100‑like, rad‑hard variant), 64 GB HBM2e each.
· FPGA Accelerators: 4× Xilinx Versal AI Core for transformer inference.
· Storage: Distributed object store, 1 PB raw sensor history.

5.3 Software Stack

· Fusion engine: Temporal fusion transformer (TFT), Bayesian change point detection.
· Framework: PyTorch, ONNX Runtime.
· Data bus: Apache Kafka (low‑latency config) over TTEthernet.

5.4 Performance Targets

· End‑to‑end fusion latency: <50 ms (95th percentile).
· Model update rate: 10 Hz full state, 100 Hz for critical telemetry.
· False alarm rate (anomaly): <1 per 24 h.

