6. Layer 6: Booster Fusion – Adaptive Resource Scheduler

6.1 Functional Requirements

· FR‑6.1 – Dynamically allocate compute (CPU/GPU/photonic/quantum) based on workload priority.
· FR‑6.2 – Reallocate electrical power between reactors, batteries, and loads.
· FR‑6.3 – Co‑optimise with thermal management system.
· FR‑6.4 – Provide API for capacity reservations.

6.2 Hardware Specification

· Scheduler Controller: 2× rad‑hard ARM Cortex‑A76, 8 cores each, lockstep.
· Power Telemetry: Current/voltage sensors on all power distribution units.
· Actuation: Solid‑state power controllers (SSPC).

6.3 Software Stack

· Scheduler: Hierarchical multi‑agent RL (PPO), trained on 10⁶ simulation years.
· Integration: ROS 2 node with DDS.
· API: RESTful over HTTPS (internal).

6.4 Performance Targets

· Scheduling decision: <1 ms.
· Power reallocation transient: <5 ms.
· Throughput: 10,000 allocation requests per second.

