7. Layer 5: Hybrid Photonic‑Electronic AI

7.1 Functional Requirements

· FR‑5.1 – Real‑time orbit determination and attitude control (1000 Hz).
· FR‑5.2 – High‑throughput encryption / quantum key distribution.
· FR‑5.3 – Real‑time video analytics for docking and spacewalk assistance.
· FR‑5.4 – Interface with electronic neuromorphic processors for slower cognition.

7.2 Hardware Specification

· Photonic Cores: Distributed reservoir computing nodes integrated into fibre backbone.
  · 1,024 optical nodes, each with SOA, delay lines, balanced photodetectors.
  · Weight programming via thermo‑optic phase shifters.
· Electronic Neuromorphic: 16× Intel Loihi‑2 (or equivalent) chips, 1M neurons each.
· Bridge: Silicon photonic transceiver, <1 ns latency.

7.3 Software Stack

· Optical reservoir: Trained offline, weights updated monthly.
· Neuromorphic: Nengo, custom SNN compiler.
· Control loop: Implemented in VHDL on photonic node FPGAs.

7.4 Performance Targets

· Attitude control latency: <0.5 ms from sensor to thruster command.
· QKD key rate: 10 Mbps.
· Video analytics (1080p, 30 fps): <5 ms end‑to‑end.

